17	commands.sync.	repo-sync.ts builds t(`commands.sync.${mode}.completed|failed|starting|progress`) where mode is upload|download; the full leaf key is never a static literal, so the upload/download subtrees are only reachable at runtime.
18	errors.term.	term.ts renders t(`errors.term.${codeKey}`) mapping an SSH exit code to a message; the per-code leaves are concatenated at runtime and never appear as a static t() literal.
19	commands.machine.health.	machine/health.ts emits t(`commands.machine.health.${field.key}`) over a runtime field list; the per-field leaves are built dynamically and never appear as a static literal.
20	commands.config.infra.push.dns	infra-provision.ts logDnsAction builds `commands.config.infra.push.dns${Created|Updated|Deleted}` from a DnsAction; the dnsCreated/dnsUpdated/dnsDeleted leaves are concatenated at runtime, not static literals.
22	docs.	the docs.* namespace is the www cli-docs generator's private vocabulary (packages/www/scripts/generate-cli-docs.js), not CLI t(); it reads docs.frontmatter directly and emits docs.* via runtime-built {{t:cli.docs.*}} the committed markdown may not fully enumerate, so a static CLI scan cannot see these references.
